WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.984 --> 00:00:02.714
- [Narrator] The creation
of the potato chip

00:00:02.714 --> 00:00:06.881
is a rather snarky, surprising,
and idiosyncratic story.

00:00:08.937 --> 00:00:11.073
When French fries made
their way to America,

00:00:11.073 --> 00:00:13.175
they soon became a restaurant mainstay.

00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:15.987
Many restaurants served Fries
as their signature dish.

00:00:15.987 --> 00:00:16.945
Believe it or not,

00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:19.560
they were once considered
very hoity-toity.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.296
In 1853, George Crum was a
chef at the Moon's Lake House

00:00:23.296 --> 00:00:25.272
in Saratoga Springs, New York.

00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:26.793
Their signature dish was none other

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:30.276
than Moon's Fried Potatoes, or
as the aristocrats would say:

00:00:30.276 --> 00:00:32.993
"Potatoes served in the French Manner."

00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:35.501
One day, just like any other,
a customer some believe

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:39.657
to have been Cornelius
Vanderbilt himself ordered fries.

00:00:39.657 --> 00:00:43.430
Upon being served, Cornelius
scoffed, and sent them back.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.219
He deemed the fries soggy
and not crispy enough.

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:50.269
This insanity continued a few
more times until Crum lost it.

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:52.277
I mean, he really lost it.

00:00:52.277 --> 00:00:54.831
He fired back, cutting
the potatoes paper-thin,

00:00:54.831 --> 00:00:56.097
and frying them up.

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:57.490
You see, back in 1853,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.824
eating with your hands
was a major faux pas,

00:00:59.824 --> 00:01:02.587
making Crum's revenge
even more diabolical.

00:01:02.587 --> 00:01:04.491
By cutting the potatoes paper-thin,

00:01:04.491 --> 00:01:07.219
there would be no way that
Cornelius could use his fork,

00:01:07.219 --> 00:01:09.274
forcing him to use his hands.

00:01:09.274 --> 00:01:11.689
Crum's plan backfired, kind of,

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:15.172
as the patrons dug in with
both hands, and loved them.

00:01:15.172 --> 00:01:17.006
Saratoga Chips were born.

00:01:17.006 --> 00:01:19.224
They became a Saratoga dining staple.

00:01:19.224 --> 00:01:21.941
Soon thereafter, they
took the world by storm.

00:01:21.941 --> 00:01:24.123
Crum himself even opened
his own restaurant

00:01:24.123 --> 00:01:28.187
with baskets of chips displayed
on each and every table.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:31.604
(cheery xylophone music)

